  \[\begin{aligned}
  E(X) &=& 3\times0.58+4\times0.21+5\times0.21 = 3.63\\
  E(Y) &=& 5\times0.59+10\times0.27+15\times0.14 = 7.75
  \end{aligned}\]

  A distribuição do produto é dada por

  \begin{longtable}[]{@{}cccccccccc@{}}
  \toprule\noalign{}
  k & 15 & 20 & 25 & 30 & 40 & 50 & 45 & 60 & 75 \\
  \midrule\noalign{}
  \endhead
  \bottomrule\noalign{}
  \endlastfoot
  P(XY = k) & 0.49 & 0.06 & 0.04 & 0.03 & 0.13 & 0.11 & 0.06 & 0.02 &
  0.06 \\
  \end{longtable}

  De modo que
  \[E(XY) = 15\times0.49+20\times0.06+25\times0.04+30\times0.03+40\times0.13+50\times0.11+45\times0.06+60\times0.02+75\times0.06 = 29.55\]
  e, portanto, \[\text{Cov}(X,Y) = E(XY)-E(X)E(Y) = 1.418.\]

